        "question": {
          ":question/id": "3aeb2bcd-0af0-5c60-a4c6-864471f98fab",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "- $P$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${p}_{31}=2\\ne 0$.\n\n- $Q$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\n- $R$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ and $R$ are diagonal matrices.",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
